## Course overview

Economics examines how individuals, firms, and governments make choices under scarcity. Students learn to think like economists - building models, weighing trade-offs, and evaluating policy using real-world evidence.

## What you will study

- **Introduction to economics**: scarcity, choice, and economic systems.
- **Microeconomics**: markets, elasticity, market failure, and government intervention.
- **Macroeconomics**: growth, unemployment, inflation, and fiscal/monetary policy.
- **The global economy**: trade, exchange rates, development, and sustainability.

## Assessment

| Component | SL | HL | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Paper 1 (extended response) | 30% | 20% | Essay-style questions |
| Paper 2 (data response) | 40% | 30% | Analysis of real-world data |
| Paper 3 (policy paper, HL) | - | 30% | Quantitative and policy questions |
| Internal Assessment | 30% | 20% | Portfolio of three commentaries on news articles |
